h1. Tech details

* bug occurs because {{UINavigationController.setViewControllers}} is called with an empty array, which essentially breaks navigation controller: all subsequent pushes stop working at all
* fix that [~accountid:60420d6730320b00696dab69] prepared fixes the bug in {{RiderNavigationController}} , so transition from WhereTo to ActiveOrder will not lead to {{setViewControllers([])}}
* but there is still a possibility that {{setViewControllers}} will be called with an empty array - in {{RiderNavigationController.executeScheduledPops}} in

{noformat}            setViewControllers(
                viewControllers.filter { views.contains($0) == false },
                animated: true
            ){noformat}
To avoid putting {{RiderNavigationController}} into a broken state, we need not pass here an empty list. I see two options:
** either pass there something like a {{[DummyViewController()]}} which will be just an empty transparent VC - we need to remove it after subsequent push or setViewControllers is called
** or just ignore setting an empty list of VCs and always keep at least one VC in there
** cc [~accountid:5f770d64837bb800682d18b3] to think about it 👆. Also, I’d suggest covering {{RiderNavVC}} with tests.



