We should have most iot configuration parameters available here for setting. Also, we have two new parameters which I think are not in the scooter.proto3 used on backend yet (those need to be added to iotStatus service as well).

the ‘city’ parameter here actually is search category id.

My current process runs as follows:

the process keeps task list. task consists of all configuration items to be changes + difference of audio files (ie files to be added and files to be deleted from the device). Each 10 minutes data about all vehicles is scanned from the redis (~ iotStatus service on backend) difference between current config on device vs expected configuration is calculated, and all scooters with difference are added to the tasklist end

tasklist is processed as a queue, having configurable maximum number of items to be processed in parallel (to not to overload whole system when something in configuration changes). each device is processed max n times , if even after n times this is unsuccessful for some reason (mostly timeouts from devices), the device is added to blacklist for 2 hours, which prevents it to be added to queue until it’s purged from blacklist.

When configuration task is successful, the set/store command is sent, so the iot stores the current parameter set on flash and loads those as default values next time it restarts.

With audio files the task processes them one-by-one, by first deleting those on the device which should not be there, then adding missing ones one-by-one. Currently audio files are stored on the disk in directories by language:


!image-20210819-080701.png|width=517,height=384!

Audio files are loaded on service startup, confirmed to be on mqtt broker, and added there if needed.

Checking presence of audio file on the device is done by filename:length, which allows easily to change the file without renaming it (ie files with same name and different length are considered to be different files)

