Hi\!

We may provide data to the police, but certain requirements should be met in order for these requests to be valid and purposeful. We, as the controller of data, need to make sure that the data given out is necessary for the purpose and also to follow the data minimisation principle. So, if the police request is too vague (eg. asking for all data about a user in bulk, not specifying the user etc), then we need to ask the police, if possible, to limit the scope and bring out the purpose why they need the data. I would think that the local criminal laws would also foresee the necessity for that.

Second, as a matter of general rule we allow our local subsidiaries/partner markets to respond to police requests directly when request for disclosure of personal data meets all the following conditions:

(a) the Personal Data is requested in connection with alleged crime;

(b) the request is presented on the law enforcement agency's letterhead;

(c) the request is duly signed and stamped by the appropriate law enforcement officer who is empowered by local law to represent the law enforcement agency that is making the request, and the Contractor has taken reasonable steps to validate the identity and authority of the officer;

(d) the request includes all the following elements: 

(i) all known email addresses, names, and phone numbers of the User(s) whose Personal Data is requested;

(ii) precise description of information requested, reasoning of why information is requested, and how it pertains to investigation of the alleged crime;

(iii) reference to applicable provisions of the relevant law under which the agency is entitled to request the information.

So, all in all, in order to give police the data it needs to be made sure whether the request is *valid* (for security purposes) and second whether the request is *purposeful and necessary.*

I can see that the request has come in on the formal letterhead, is stamped and signed. 

They have also brought out the alleged crime in connection to which they need the data. If they are asking about the user who made the specific trip, then this is purposeful and necessary for the investigation. 

Let us know if you have any more questions before proceeding with the request.

