This is the advice we have received from outside counsel on the lease for the new Portugal Store:

The agreement is generally market standard so no immediate risks. However outside counsel has included some provisions to safeguard our position as tenant. 

An explanation of outside counsel’s suggested amendments as in Section A below (which you may wish to forward to the other side for more context. 

Please can you send this over to the landlord and their lawyer and copy me in? I will deal with them direct thereafter.

*A.*    +*Amendments*+:

* Clause 1: inclusion of reference to use permit and energy certificate of the property, and to be included as Annexes to the agreement;
* Clause 4/4: reduction of the days to return the deposit (from 30 to 10 days) and clearer wording on costs that can be deducted from that deposit (deposit can be deducted from damages +that are the responsibility+ of the tenant);
* Clause 5/2: inclusion of a termination provision if the licensing of the property is not compatible with the activity of the tenant (i.e. the tenant can terminate the agreement if the use permit of the leased premises is not, or stops being, compatible with the activity you are carrying out);
* Clause 5/3: parties to conduct a survey on the property before the start of the agreement, making sure they are in agreement with the state of condition of the property, and signing a document attesting that;
* Clause 7/3: inclusion of a provision stating that the tenant can remove any works or improvements done on the property that are not permanently connected to the property;
* Clause 7/4: inclusion of provision stating that the landlord is responsible for carrying out the indispensable works for the conservation and repair of the structural elements of the leased premises;
* Clause 8/2: clarification that the landlord is responsible for condominium expenses and expenses +with the common areas of the property+;
* Clause 9/1: removal of the obligation of the tenant to maintain the conservation state of plumbing, electricity and sewers. We can accept walls, painting or windows, but what is inside the walls should not be your responsibility;
* Clause 10: inclusion of the obligation of the landlord to have mandatory insurances regarding the property;
* Clause 11/1: upon the final inspection of the leased premises by the landlord, +it should be accompanied by the tenant+ (or a representative); and
* Clause 12/1: obligation to send copies via email of all communications sent by letter.

